{"name":"Marine Layer","hex":"#a5b4b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Belonging to or characteristic of the sea; existing or found in the sea; formed or produced by the sea.","Relating to or connected with the sea (in operation, scope, etc.), especially as pertains to shipping, a navy, or naval forces."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soldier, normally a member of a marine corps, trained to serve on board or from a ship.",": A marine corps."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marine"},{"term":"layer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A single thickness of some material covering a surface.","An item of clothing worn under or over another."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cut or divide into layers.","To arrange in layers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/layer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marine layer","blocks":[{"text":"A marine layer is an air mass that develops over the surface of a large body of water, such as an ocean or large lake, in the presence of a temperature inversion. The inversion itself is usually initiated by the cooling effect caused when cold water on the surface of the ocean interacts with a comparatively warm air mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/San_francisco_in_fog_with_rays.jpg/330px-San_francisco_in_fog_with_rays.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marine_layer","wikidata":"Q6764294"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Marine_layer_from_Mount_Wilson.jpg/500px-Marine_layer_from_Mount_Wilson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Marine_layer_from_Mount_Wilson.jpg/1280px-Marine_layer_from_Mount_Wilson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Marine_layer_from_Mount_Wilson.jpg/500px-Marine_layer_from_Mount_Wilson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Coastal marine layer filling the Los Angeles Basin in May, as viewed from Mount Wilson. In Southern California, April and May typically have the highest prevalence of marine layer.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarine_layer_from_Mount_Wilson.jpg"}],"sounds":{"marine":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e5/En-us-marine.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e5/En-us-marine.ogg/En-us-marine.ogg.mp3"}],"layer":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fa/En-us-layer.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fa/En-us-layer.ogg/En-us-layer.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fa/En-us-layer.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fa/En-us-layer.ogg/En-us-layer.ogg.mp3"}]}}}